infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Projecting the read model: sync vs async
  desc The core design choice — consistency in the write transaction, or a lean write path with bounded staleness
  compares
    - label Synchronous projection
      children
        - label Runs in the write transaction
          desc Read model updated atomically with the write
        - label Always consistent
          desc Read model never lags the write side
        - label Slower write path
          desc Txn also completes the read-model update
        - label Projection failure fails the command
          desc One transaction boundary spans both concerns
        - label Each read model lengthens the txn
          desc Best for one small, fast read model
    - label Asynchronous projection
      children
        - label Runs after the write commits
          desc Separate process via event bus or CDC
        - label Eventually consistent
          desc Staleness window Δ — ms to low seconds
        - label Lean, fast write path
          desc Command commits the write side only
        - label Decoupled from the write
          desc Projection retries without blocking writes
        - label Independent projection workers
          desc Many read models scaled and deployed apart
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
